# WAIO Segment Recovery MVP (Phase 49) -- segment registry.
# format: SEGMENT_ID|HOST|PORT|WORKER_NAME|LABEL
#   SEGMENT_ID  - stable identifier for this segment (also used as its
#                 state-file name and audit log key; no spaces/pipes)
#   HOST        - address health_checker.sh probes (TCP connect only)
#   PORT        - port to probe (the SSH port for every segment so far)
#   WORKER_NAME - the workers/registry.conf NAME this segment corresponds
#                 to (documentation/cross-reference only; the health
#                 checker never dispatches through waio.sh itself, it
#                 only opens a raw TCP connection -- see
#                 security/health_checker.sh's header for why)
#   LABEL       - free-form description (documentation only)
# lines starting with # and blank lines are ignored.
#
# This is an example/template (same Public / Private Security Boundary
# pattern as security/egress_allowlist.conf.example, Phase 29). Copy it
# to security/segments.conf and fill in this deployment's real segments
# -- see README.md's Setup section. The real file is gitignored.
#
# Unlike egress_allowlist.conf, an empty or missing segments.conf is
# NOT a security-relevant fail-closed condition -- it just means no
# segments are currently monitored. security/segment_manager.sh still
# requires the file to exist (a clear "not configured yet" error
# instead of silently doing nothing), but zero valid entries in an
# existing file is a valid, safe state, not a bypass of anything.
HOST800|REPLACE_WITH_HOST800_IP|22|HOST800|800号機
RPI|REPLACE_WITH_RPI_IP|22|RPI|Raspberry Pi
